meta {
  name: update-category
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

patch {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/menu/categories/{{category_uid}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "description": "Clear, thick and seasonal"
  }
}

tests {
  test("responds 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200)
  })

  test("envelope reports success", function () {
    // Asserting on `code`, not `message`: codes are stable, messages are human copy that will be
    // translated (PRD section 7).
    expect(res.body.code).to.equal("00000")
  })
}

docs {
  # Update a category

PATCH semantics: omitted fields are left alone, and a field sent as `""` clears it. That distinction
is why the request DTO uses pointers.

Archiving a category that still holds dishes is refused (`TX_MNU_003`) rather than cascading --
cascading would delete menu items that order history references.
}
